WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.480
I'm here from Aquarium Tingaara for training.

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.150
My name is Haebaru Chiyu.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:06.840
I'll be in your care.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.400
Aquarium Tingaara?

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:14.940
That's the new aquarium that's opening 
next year in the city center.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.120
Right.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.810
Would you like to join someone 
in our daily duties?

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.860
How about Kukuru?

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.920
You're the acting director, after all.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.840
I look forward to your instruction.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.470
<b>Upkeep Record</b>

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:10.350
Why is a rival bringing someone 
to Gama Gama to study?

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.280
They aren't really rivals.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:15.840
Aquariums tend to help each other out.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:21.070
I hear the staff at Tingaara all go 
to different aquariums to study.

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:22.370
Isn't that great?

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:25.930
There's something exciting 
about a new aquarium.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:27.500
What a pain in the ass.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.300
I hope Kukuru's going to be all right.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:37.630
I see.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.800
A new aquarium, huh?

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.680
Misakino-san, may I participate?

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:49.540
You just need these ones 
chopped up small, right?

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.940
Will that do?

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:01.120
Yes.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:03.770
These are going to the animals 
in the main tank, right?

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:05.160
Y-Yeah.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:08.060
Since there are all kinds of animals there, 
we chop them in different sizes

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:09.690
so it's easier to eat.

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:12.280
So that the smaller fish can eat it, too.

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:14.430
You have different kinds, too, huh?

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:15.070
Yeah.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:16.650
We have different kinds.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:18.630
Do you know what we're
feeding them today?

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.820
I don't know how great
the new aquarium is,

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:26.880
but if you're going to work here, 
this is common sense.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.040
Brit,

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:33.270
opossum shrimp, blue-sprat, squid, mackerel.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.440
Is that right?

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.000
H-Hey, as long as you know.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:43.490
I was quite sure I knew, 
but it's good to learn on-site again.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:45.990
Thank you!

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:52.270
You can get to the back 
of the main tank through here.

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:52.960
Right!

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.970
It's a Cinderella sea slug!

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.500
It's so cute.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.260
You recognize it?

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:01.200
Yes!

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.680
With its colorful pinks, it's like a flower
blooming on the bottom of the sea.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:08.800
I hear they're difficult to raise, though.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:10.200
They are!

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:12.970
We finally figured out how to raise them, 
after a lot of trouble!

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.690
We'll take a short break 
after we're done with feeding.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:19.580
Got it.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:28.910
<b>Customers are ahead.</b>

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:28.910
<b>Don't forget to smile!</b>

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:27.030
<i>Why do I have to be so good 
to the enemy?</i>

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:28.910
<i>Gramps, you idiot!</i>

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:33.550
<i>Everyone over here is nice.</i>

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:35.250
<i>And training is really fun.</i>

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.390
Yeah? Good for you.

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:38.820
<i>How about you?</i>

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.850
I don't know yet.

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:45.200
<i>Didn't they say there's 
a legendary aquarium keeper there?</i>

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.010
Oh.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:47.900
It's true, but...

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:53.980
I'm sending you to Gama Gama.

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:58.060
You said you preferred 
somewhere nearby, right?

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:02.220
But Gama Gama is the one 
that's closing soon, isn't it?

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:05.530
It seems to me 
I'd be learning from failure.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:06.700
No, no.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.690
You're new, so you may not know,

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:14.670
but the director at Gama Gama's been called 
the "legendary aquarium keeper."

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:15.710
Legendary?

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:16.940
Yeah.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:21.150
He's been to aquariums all over.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:24.650
He's been able to present all kinds
of animals that are difficult to raise.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:27.530
And he's saved failing aquariums 
with unique events.

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:29.710
He has a long résumé of successes.

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:30.960
Huh.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:35.380
I'm sure you'll learn a lot 
by watching him work.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.200
All right.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:42.230
I'll go see for myself 
whether he's really that amazing.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:47.600
I thought I'd get to learn from
the legendary aquarium keeper,

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:51.420
but the equipment is falling apart, 
and things are just really meh.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:54.750
<i>Guess you'll have to live with it 
until training's over, then.</i>

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.030
<i>Hang in there.</i>

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:57.130
Thanks.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:05:58.460
See you.

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:06.260
How are the feet?

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:10.520
Yeah, I think they're all good.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:12.510
Let's get back to walking, then.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:15.270
Good for you, Choko-san!

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.270
We're off break!

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:21.110
We're about to walk the penguins.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:25.440
There isn't anything for you to do, 
so you can just follow us.

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:29.440
I can at least guide the guests, though.

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:32.240
I don't think there are 
that many guests here, anyway.

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:36.520
We wouldn't want for anything 
to go wrong, though.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:38.090
We don't get many guests here?

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:38.940
Was that an insult?

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:39.710
Kukuru!

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:47.800
You can come see the penguins 
close up, Haebaru-san.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:48.760
Right.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:50.110
Thank you!

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:51.110
I will.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:55.280
Are you sure?

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:59.050
What if the penguins attack her as they
did me, and she falls into the tank?

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:00.800
That'll be a good teaching moment.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:01.770
Kukuru!

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:03.000
There, there.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:04.020
Good kids.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:08.170
Haebaru-san, they're going to peck
at you if you try to touch them!

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:09.610
You shouldn't agitate them!

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:11.430
Oh, really?

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:15.410
Maybe I should stand back a little.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:18.860
They peck at people 
who they aren't used to, huh?

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:21.040
That sounds just like Misakino-san.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:23.870
Haebaru-san!

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:25.420
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:28.050
You said not to agitate them.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:29.920
I'll be careful going forward.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:33.960
I'm sure she didn't mean anything by it.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:36.010
She obviously did!

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:41.210
Time to walk the penguins!

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:45.450
These penguins are known as Cape penguins.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:48.520
You can recognize them by
the black line under their beaks,

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:51.780
and the dots on their bellies.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:56.760
The name Cape penguin comes 
from the Cape area of South Africa.

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:59.290
They're the only species 
of penguin in Africa.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:03.870
They're known to bite 
when they're threatened,

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:09.020
but all the kids at Gama Gama 
walk happily together!

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:15.300
All the kids walk happily together!

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:21.100
I'm getting bad vibes.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:24.460
Kukuru's clearly in a bad mood.

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:28.010
What are you doing?

00:08:28.010 --> 00:08:31.110
The air's so bad 
that I'm suffocating.

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:33.260
What are you, a fish?

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:36.370
<b>Welcome to Gama Gama Aquarium</b>

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:39.420
Man, I'm starving!

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.250
Good work today.

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:42.770
<b>Sunday, August 22nd</b>

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:42.770
<b>Notification Center

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.220
Fuuka, come on, hurry up!

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:49.880
Let's go eat.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:53.020
I'm so hungry.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:54.010
<b>Cinderella, the Spy</b>

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:58.420
Why can't you get along with her?

00:08:58.420 --> 00:08:59.970
How could I?

00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:01.790
Why not?

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:05.880
I don't want the new aquarium 
to take our guests.

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:07.800
It doesn't matter.

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:11.690
If more people get to see the sea creatures 
and get to love them just a little,

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:13.720
that's all that matters, right?

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:18.120
You might be okay with that, 
but it has to be Gama Gama for me.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:19.950
It's true, isn't it?

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:21.700
Grams?

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:28.120
You don't know anything about
other aquariums, do you, Kukuru?

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:34.590
It's important to have even a little
compassion for what's unfamiliar to you.

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:38.940
You both love aquariums.

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:42.310
It'll be more fun if you can get along.

00:09:44.530 --> 00:09:48.320
I don't know anymore.

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:49.190
Yeah.

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:55.320
Am I trying to protect Gama Gama?

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.950
Or am I just clinging to my memories?

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:03.950
I think it's okay either way.

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:10.100
You care about Gama Gama, 
and I support that.

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:11.850
Thanks.

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:15.960
But I think your attitude today wasn't great.

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:21.160
I wish you would have been more steady, 
as the acting director.

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:23.980
I'll be more careful.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:30.220
I'd be tarnishing Gama
Gama's reputation if I act up.

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:31.420
Exactly!

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:32.360
Be strong!

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:37.530
Hey...

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:41.570
Can I ask you a weird question?

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:43.700
What?

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:51.620
Sometimes, I wish I had 
an older sister like you.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:54.040
We're the same age, though.

00:10:56.180 --> 00:11:01.340
There are some things that my parents 
cherished in the family altar drawer.

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:09.590
Apparently, you get one maternity
handbook for every child you have.

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:14.630
So one's for me, 
and I don't know about the other.

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:17.260
What does Grams say?

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:19.400
I can't ask her.

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.850
I'm kind of scared.

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:25.500
But I keep imagining...

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:30.330
Maybe I have siblings 
that I've never met.

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:34.710
And for some reason, 
we've had to live apart.

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:42.060
I bet it'd make me really happy 
if I suddenly had an older sister.

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:43.220
You'd be happy?

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:44.960
I would be.

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:46.570
I'd have more family.

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:51.530
That's my weird talk.

00:11:52.460 --> 00:11:54.140
Let's hold hands in bed tonight.

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:56.570
It's okay. Don't worry about me!

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:58.190
I want to!

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:00.190
Jeez, that's embarrassing.

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:01.370
You're so mean!

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:02.480
I'm kidding.

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:03.530
Sorry.

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:05.460
I don't care about you anymore.

00:12:36.260 --> 00:12:37.480
Hello!

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:41.440
Kamee's special lunch boxes are here.

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:44.280
Today on the menu is salt-grilled mackerel.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.640
Is that her?

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:49.400
Yeah.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:51.260
She's here for training, from Tingaara.

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:53.630
I think I'll go say "hi."

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:56.320
Director, may I have a word?

00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:58.250
Sure, what is it?

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:03.010
I'd like for you to tutor me 
from the afternoon, if it's possible.

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.580
My boss told me, too.

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:09.010
To go see the work 
of the legendary aquarium keeper.

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:10.880
Legendary aquarium keeper?

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:14.140
Yeah, that's what they used 
to call the director.

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:16.270
What do you think, Kukuru?

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:18.770
I don't mind either way.

00:13:19.180 --> 00:13:20.200
All right.

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:22.620
Let's switch, then.

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:24.170
Thank you!

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:25.530
Hello!

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:27.450
I came to deliver lunch.

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:30.530
I'm Teruya Tsukimi, from Kamee Diner.

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:34.570
Would you like to order something 
for tomorrow, too, miss?

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:36.060
No, thanks.

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:41.590
She's so blunt.

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:49.300
From noon today, huh?

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:50.430
Yes.

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:53.540
There isn't really anything 
to do in particular.

00:13:55.860 --> 00:14:01.230
<i>He just looks like some
old retired guy killing time.</i>

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:03.920
<i>But he's the legendary aquarium keeper.</i>

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:09.170
<i>He must be casually checking
the fish along the way.</i>

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:09.740
Hey.

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:12.700
<i>The legend has noticed something!</i>

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:16.910
Oh, you finally got a rare card.

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:17.660
Yup.

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:19.050
That's amazing.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.420
Show me again next time.

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:22.860
Okay!

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:28.640
Why are those kids playing
card games at an aquarium?

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:33.150
The kids with annual passes 
come here all the time.

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:35.890
They've gotten bored already.

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:43.930
You're guests! Why are you...

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:49.470
I'm sorry. I made a bit of a mess, 
so we're borrowing the cleaning equipment.

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:52.960
I'm sorry. We shouldn't
be making guests clean.

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:54.700
It's all right.

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:56.990
We've got plenty of time, anyway.

00:14:56.990 --> 00:14:58.140
I'm sorry.

00:14:58.140 --> 00:15:00.090
Thanks for everything.

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:03.780
Gramps really likes 
to work people to the bone.

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:09.130
So we're getting married.

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:13.010
We came home for Obon, 
so we thought you'd let you know.

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:15.510
Good for you.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:17.260
Are you keeping busy?

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:19.470
All the time, lately.

00:15:19.470 --> 00:15:22.340
We're trucking dirt around 
all day, every day.

00:15:22.340 --> 00:15:23.020
Is that so?

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:27.140
The guests here aren't
even looking at the fish.

00:15:28.770 --> 00:15:30.280
I've had enough.

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:33.830
I don't think there's anything more 
to learn from there.

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:34.530
<i>What?</i>

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:38.680
It was a mistake to come 
to an aquarium that's about to close.

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:41.260
May I go train somewhere else?

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:42.670
<i>Listen...</i>

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.520
I got taught by a high-schooler!

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:47.300
You don't think that's too half-assed?

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:49.760
<i>That's a bit much, but...</i>

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:54.920
I want to spend the rest of my time 
training properly at a different aquarium.

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:56.330
Please!

00:15:58.690 --> 00:15:59.850
<i>Fine.</i>

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:02.620
<i>I'll talk to another aquarium.</i>

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:05.940
<i>I'll apologize to the director 
of Gama Gama for you.</i>

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:08.780
Please and thank you.

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:18.340
You have no idea how hard
it was to get this far.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.580
What we like about Gama Gama?

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:22.590
Yeah.

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:26.110
Something about it that makes it even more
awesome than a brand-new, fancy aquarium.

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:27.340
Is there anything?

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:29.340
The cheap entry fee!

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:33.720
Something weird happened, though.

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:35.930
That was really cool!

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:37.930
What happened?

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:40.730
I saw the dog I used to have.

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:41.690
Here.

00:16:45.550 --> 00:16:47.390
That was really nostalgic!

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:48.880
Are you sure?

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:50.500
Really?

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:52.250
I called his name, 
and he was wagging his tail.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:05.370
I'm done training today.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:07.310
Already?

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:08.360
Yes.

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:12.310
I don't think I was a good fit here.

00:17:12.310 --> 00:17:14.590
What do you mean by "not a good fit"?

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:19.600
I was trained by a high schooler, 
people were chatting all day on site...

00:17:19.980 --> 00:17:22.620
It felt like a waste of time.

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:27.710
The director is trying 
to teach you something deeper.

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:30.330
Not that a shallow-minded person
like you would understand,

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:33.990
coming to conclusions after just two days.

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:43.400
You may be having fun play-working, 
but I'm desperate.

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:44.280
<i>"Play"?</i>

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:45.240
That's right.

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:47.100
Thousands of people look 
for employment every year,

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:49.520
after graduating from
technical schools and colleges.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:53.490
Meanwhile, there are only about 
a hundred aquariums around Japan.

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:56.170
Do you know how few of them are hiring?

00:17:56.660 --> 00:17:59.890
I made it through a narrow
window to finally get here.

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:03.990
I don't want to let go of the job 
that I earned for myself.

00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:07.770
So I want proper training. That's all.

00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:13.090
You're still in high school 
and helping out the family business, correct?

00:18:13.090 --> 00:18:15.930
You don't know what it's like 
to have to make money.

00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:17.690
You're underestimating things.

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:26.040
It wasn't for very long, 
but thank you for your time.

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:27.960
Excuse me.

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:39.350
Hey.

00:18:39.990 --> 00:18:42.410
I'm done with work early today. 
I'll see you.

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:48.190
Kai!

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:50.070
Give me a hand!

00:18:50.070 --> 00:18:51.810
Fine, fine.

00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:53.610
I hate her!

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:55.320
Never come back, you evil spirit!

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:56.610
Damn it!

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:58.270
I can't stand it!

00:18:58.270 --> 00:19:00.160
You're so immature.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:02.240
That's what she said, too!

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:05.980
You underestimate me.

00:19:05.980 --> 00:19:07.580
Small fish in a big pond.

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:13.130
And you're swimming with sharks.

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:14.240
Ow!

00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:16.710
This better be part of my pay.

00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:18.910
Challenge!

00:19:18.910 --> 00:19:19.510
Ack.

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:20.620
Hang on.

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:21.510
Nope.

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:25.020
Are you two not going 
to look at the fish?

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:27.020
No, we aren't.

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:28.470
We already know them all!

00:19:29.190 --> 00:19:33.790
Those ones in the deep sea tank 
are spiny lobster, big roughy,

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:35.980
Bathynomus doederleinii, 
Japanese spider crab.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:41.050
In the reef tank are a bicolor angelfish, 
blueface angelfish, brown tang,

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:46.810
lemon damsel, amethyst anthias, honeycomb toby, 
blue tang, yellow longnose butterflyfish.

00:19:46.810 --> 00:19:48.120
That's not right.

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:51.660
The yellow longnose butterflyfish got moved 
to the welcome tank, remember?

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:53.630
Really? When did that happen?

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:58.090
The guests here aren't
even looking at the fish.

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:03.320
Of course you are.

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:14.900
Thank you.

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.810
Come back soon.

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:20.780
Say "hi" to the director at Tingaara for me.

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:21.990
Okay.

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:35.080
I'm never coming back.

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:42.220
Thanks for waiting.

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:43.920
Sorry, Fuuka.

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:45.860
I'll be home later.

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:48.040
I need to stop by somewhere.

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:50.550
Tell them I won't need dinner.

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:08.800
Where did Kukuru say she's going?

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:11.270
She hasn't told me anything.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.060
<b>Shiroi Ruka
Mobile</b>

00:21:15.010 --> 00:21:16.180
Aren't you going to answer?

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:23.550
Yes?

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:25.520
<i>Fuuka-senpai, is that you?</i>

00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:26.520
<i>It's been a long time.</i>

00:21:26.520 --> 00:21:28.360
<i>Thank goodness I got a hold of you.</i>

00:21:28.360 --> 00:21:29.680
Ruka-chan?

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:31.950
<i>Sorry for calling you so many times.</i>

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:33.640
<i>Do you have a moment?</i>

00:21:33.950 --> 00:21:35.640
Sure, I do.

00:21:36.050 --> 00:21:37.190
Is something wrong?

00:21:37.920 --> 00:21:41.190
<i>There's something 
I really want to tell you.</i>

00:23:21.750 --> 00:23:23.750
<b>Construction Permit</b>

00:23:21.750 --> 00:23:23.750
<b>Building name  Aquarium Tingaara</b>

00:23:21.750 --> 00:23:23.750
<b>Business name  Kaleva Resort Group</b>
